{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1240180-imbued-item-merit-spell-with-resources","id":1240180,"title":"Imbued Item Merit/Spell with Resources","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-07-29T12:57:37-07:00","id":1240180,"title":"Imbued Item Merit/Spell with Resources","content":"Hi!<br /> <br /> I found many discutions about the Merit and Spell envolving this, but my actual problem is quite different. We are playing a medieval fantasy campaign and we created a houserule to acquire magic itens (imbued) with coins during the game (Resources). The cost is working good and the difficult based on rarity of the effect is ok either. The problem is: now there is a mage player that want the Primal to create itens for other players. How to deal with this? If he is allowed to create imbued itens &quot;at will&quot; , I see that this could make the game unbalanced, with each player like a &quot;Christmas tree&quot; of magic itens without any cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9723-winchester","name":"winchester","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T13:52:52-07:00","id":1240205,"title":"","content":"If by &quot;at will&quot; you mean &quot;with the expenditure of time and resources that comes with ritual spellcasting that often means not being involved in the other prep work of other things happening&quot;, sure.<br /> <br /> If by at will you mean &quot;Now I can have all the magic swords all willy nilly&quot;, then no. It's a process to make imbued items, and that needs to be kept to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T15:03:41-07:00","id":1240225,"title":"","content":"I play an artificer in my current Pathfinder game, and it's never been a problem. Just keep track of the costs (especially Mana), and you should be fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T16:47:40-07:00","id":1240243,"title":"","content":"Also remember that the Imbuement is sitting on your Spell Control, so there is your Gnosis as a cap on the total &quot;enchanted&quot;. You can Relinquish, but doing that safely requires a Willpower <b>dot</b>, which takes 1XP to buy back.<br /> <br /> (No one is really sure what happens when you unsafely Reliquish Imbued Items, but I'd guess &quot;cursed&quot; could be used as a description.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T09:59:22-07:00","id":1240485,"title":"","content":"The players are already \u201ca Christmas tree\u201d of magic powers. Adding items to the mix isn\u2019t going to make things worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T11:20:49-07:00","id":1240523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1240180-imbued-item-merit-spell-with-resources?p=1240243#post1240243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also remember that the Imbuement is sitting on your Spell Control, so there is your Gnosis as a cap on the total &amp;quot;enchanted&amp;quot;. You can Relinquish, but doing that safely requires a Willpower <b>dot</b>, which takes 1XP to buy back.<br /> <br /> (No one is really sure what happens when you unsafely Reliquish Imbued Items, but I'd guess &amp;quot;cursed&amp;quot; could be used as a description.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Addendum, though this isn't about <i>making</i> the Imbued Items: Each use has a minimum Mana cost of 1, so it isn't like this is free magic. Even if the crafter makes an armory of magic gear, powering all of that is going to get prohibitive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T16:06:49-07:00","id":1240625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1240180-imbued-item-merit-spell-with-resources?p=1240243#post1240243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also remember that the Imbuement is sitting on your Spell Control, so there is your Gnosis as a cap on the total &quot;enchanted&quot;. You can Relinquish, but doing that safely requires a Willpower <b>dot</b>, which takes 1XP to buy back.<br /> <br /> (No one is really sure what happens when you unsafely Reliquish Imbued Items, but I'd guess &quot;cursed&quot; could be used as a description.)</div> </div> </div> </div>But Relinquishing a Spell is ALWAYS 1 dot of Willpower, no matter if the effect is a Spell of Arcana 1 or 5, or an effect with Potency 1 or 5, right? Don't you think that must have something additional to balance this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9723-winchester","name":"winchester","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T16:26:51-07:00","id":1240631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>winchester</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1240180-imbued-item-merit-spell-with-resources?p=1240625#post1240625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Relinquishing a Spell is ALWAYS 1 dot of Willpower, no matter if the effect is a Spell of Arcana 1 or 5, or an effect with Potency 1 or 5, right? Don't you think that must have something additional to balance this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Safely Relinquishing is always a dot (Unsafely is merely a point). As to the Arcana Rating - at a certain point, what does it matter? How many effects do you really want permanent, and you with no control over the spell's remaining effects?<br /> <br /> Now, as to the equivalent XP costs - Imbued Items are more expensive Merit-dot wise than making the same Item and just Relinquishing it yourself (provided you have access to the necessary Arcana). Imbued spells can have ridiculous Spell Factors when Imbued, none of which are applicable afterwards - Imbued Items always use the same Gnosis + Arcana pool. Imbued Item's spells don't use Spell Control - Sure that nigh-Permanent Augmenting The Form you Imbued into a ring takes up one Spell Control (unless you Relinquish), but provided it has the Mana capacity, you can Buff an entire village.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T13:25:22-07:00","id":1242470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1240180-imbued-item-merit-spell-with-resources?p=1240631#post1240631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Safely Relinquishing is always a dot (Unsafely is merely a point). As to the Arcana Rating - at a certain point, what does it matter? How many effects do you really want permanent, and you with no control over the spell's remaining effects?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>i know in first edition their was some alternate method to safely relinquish a spell, can't these method be adapted for 2e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12871-elggur","name":"Elggur","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T16:21:22-07:00","id":1242524,"title":"","content":"Up to the ST, really. There is also the &quot;let a Sleepwalker you have a connection with carry it&quot; method.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T07:31:05-07:00","id":1243499,"title":"","content":"At the risk of suggesting something plain insane, couldn't someone use Mind to augment the Prime mage's resolve so that the extra willpower would make relinquishing become free ? Or would that be gone once the spell ended, along with the imbued effect ? Is there an official ruling on that ? On a related querry, when you increase resolve, do the extra willpower dots appear empty or full ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 08-07-2018, 10:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T08:22:03-07:00","id":1243509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1240180-imbued-item-merit-spell-with-resources?p=1243499#post1243499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the risk of suggesting something plain insane, couldn't someone use Mind to augment the Prime mage's resolve so that the extra willpower would make relinquishing become free ? Or would that be gone once the spell ended, along with the imbued effect ? Is there an official ruling on that ? On a related querry, when you increase resolve, do the extra willpower dots appear empty or full ?</div> </div> </div> </div>There isn\u2019t, but it seems unlikely you are supposed to be able to game the system like that. Also just having extra dots doesn\u2019t mean you\u2019ve done anything to fill them. They only start out at full between stories or at the start of a chronicle because it\u2019s assumed you\u2019ve been getting the chance to refill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T09:07:52-07:00","id":1243519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1240180-imbued-item-merit-spell-with-resources?p=1243499#post1243499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the risk of suggesting something plain insane, couldn't someone use Mind to augment the Prime mage's resolve so that the extra willpower would make relinquishing become free ? Or would that be gone once the spell ended, along with the imbued effect ? Is there an official ruling on that ? On a related querry, when you increase resolve, do the extra willpower dots appear empty or full ?</div> </div> </div> </div>With temporarily increased Health, damage persists even if it enters the temporary boxes (and may cause roll-over - I'm not sure). On the same token, spent Willpower dots probably persist after your Willpower lowers.<br /> <br /> (I've debated treating spent Willpower more like a stackable Persistent Condition, with each reducing Willpower by 1 and Resolvable via XP)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}